abstract: >
  A calibrated simulator of mobile-game real-time-bidding auctions that retains
  the ground truth for every auction, won or lost, and a benchmark built on it.
  Funnel outcomes and the top competing bid are generated on all rows, including
  the auctions the DSP lost, which no real advertising log records. Two censoring
  operators reduce the one master table to four views (C1-C4) mimicking what real
  platforms hold: a demand-side platform alone, plus measurement (MMP) data, plus
  auction price (SSP) data, and all three combined. The same two-tier bidding
  algorithm is trained under each view and scored against the retained truth and
  an oracle ceiling, so the ablation isolates each data layer's marginal
  predictive and economic value; external methods plug into the same harness.
  Software is MIT licensed; data, including the deposited datasets, is CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - real-time bidding
  - computational advertising
  - synthetic data
  - causal inference
  - selection bias
  - censored data
  - counterfactual evaluation
  - benchmark
